cy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:88e0078b3286fbc1914cc8de50982fff7c2a2ff11997f7a031826aa88234f19d","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T12:39:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T12:39:51Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1218-v0.12.18/m12stage18-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1218-v0.12.18","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1218-v0.12.18","body":"# Engacer OS M12.18 / 0.12.18 — Final desktop qualification\n\nM12-STAGE18-VM-v1 native qualification passes for these exact media.\nThis release freezes the final named-VM M12 desktop/setup regression;\npublic source, download and website checks close separately in the delivery workflow.\n\nBuild: `8ee102351039d96f68637a9edbff597b`.\nISO SHA256: `f63b78973c9da269b4eead46873d947e94fcd2266dff4b4c06f2666b743aa3f9`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `dafd107340e11ea74898c4c7ffab45dc4e31b50856421076e0b2f4787ee5bed4`.\n\n## What is delivered\n\nA real eight-step graphical installation and native desktop with original icons,\nsingle-selection/double-open, common folder navigation, reviewed file operations,\nshared dialogs, local Start search/pins/categories, grouped taskbar and window\nswitching/snap/restore. Base tray/providers, Settings and accessibility remain\nindependent of removable optional apps. High-contrast picker/notification edges\nnow have contrasting outlines without adding fixed state or a new worker.\n\n[Install](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/docs/handbook/install-m1218.md), [final guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/docs/handbook/final-m1218.md),\n[how and why](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/docs/architecture/final-m1218.md),\n[acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/evidence/M12/18/acceptance-results.json),\n[resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/evidence/M12/18/resources.json).\n\n## Fresh qualification\n\n599 compiled inputs and 184 native task/profile checks match the exact ISO/ZIP.\nFourteen enabled-device VMware profiles cover SATA, IDE, LSI Logic, LSI SAS 1068,\nPVSCSI and NVMe with BIOS/UEFI, BusLogic with BIOS, and the exact SATA/UEFI starter.\nEach installs, resets with media retained, and boots twice without the ISO or\nforced firmware order. The original supported 7-Zip console MSI lifecycle\ninstalls/runs/archives/extracts/removes/reinstalls, with 106 original payload hashes\nand independent archive/document comparison.\n\nReal setup/partition consent/failure/retry/recovery, minimal apps, desktop/files/\ntransfers/dialogs, Start/taskbar/multitasking/tray, Settings/accessibility and\nindependent USB/PS2 startup pass. Compact, 150% and actual 3840×2160/200% frames\nare separate native captures. Named USB/keyboard/hub/low-memory/larger-cluster\nround trips and real malformed/read-only/I/O/quota refusals pass their scoped gates.\n\nTwelve new BIOS/AHCI installs in three batches of four concurrent guests and\n24 independent disk-only starts pass with distinct images and exact stored guide\nbytes. The older M12.2 observation remains historical; its trigger is not claimed\nidentified and this repeat cannot prove universal reliability.\n\nFixed shell state stays 553,452 bytes (+0), with unchanged fonts and zero completed\nmanaged-page retention. Twelve default-effect cached/full comparisons and three\nEscape-cancelled move profiles restore exact native pixels. The carried production\nraster is equivalent in 3,073 host cases. Host timings are not FPS or physical-device\nbenchmarks. All CPUs halt at idle in the named native tasks.\n\n## Limits and website\n\nThe 64-MiB QEMU UEFI topology with USB storage attached before firmware boot remains\nan explicit loader refusal; the late-attachment low-memory profile passes. Public\nunsigned media keep Secure Boot off. Advanced partition tools retain logical\n1024×768. No physical/ARM/universal hardware, vendor GPU 3D, general Windows\ninstaller support, external screen-reader protocol or human usability-study result\nis introduced. Earlier stages do not qualify these new bytes.\n\nThe owned Brix recovery page uses Engacer OS and canonical documentation/download/\nGitHub links; actual hydrated email sharing uses the custom domain. No shared\nBrixCanvas platform deployment is required. Final public readback checks the native\nhomepage Save, manuals, downloads, search, mobile, archives and HTTP links.\n\n![Actual native 4K Files browsing a real owned USB folder](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/07743f643687544bb21dcd92a53a993141560cdd/evidence/M12/18/feature.png)\n"}